  "problem": "The number of deer in a wildlife reserve, measured in hundreds, is given by the function $D(t)$, where $t$ is the time, in years, since the study began. The values of $D(t)$ for several values of $t$ are shown in the table below:\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $D(t)$ | $5$ | $7$ | $10$ | $14$ | $19$ |\n\nApproximate the rate of change of the deer population when $t=4$ using a backward difference approximation. Do not round the answer.\n\nThe estimated rate of change when $t=4$ is\n{{field-1}} hundreds per year.",
